Get-Alias 
  This will let you see all the built in aliases and which powershell commands they map to. 

cls 
  This will clear your screen. 

Get-Command -Name Get-Alias 
  Get-Command will allow you to see a list of every command powershell is aware of. (Page 6)

Get-Command -Verb Get
  Using this parameter on Get-Command, you can limit hige list of commands to only those that use the Get verb

Get-Command -Verb Get -Noun Content
  If the results are too narrow, the verb can be removed. 

Get-Command -Noun Content 
  This is to show that verb and noun commands can be separated

Get-Command -Name Get-Content 
  If you'd rather define the entire command as one unit, you can use the name parameter instead and specify the entire command name. 

Get-Help Add-Content
  You can pass the command name to the Get-Help command to retrieve the standard SYNOPSIS, SYNTAX, DESCRIPTION, RELATED LINKS, and REMARKS help sections. 

Get-Help Add-Content Examples
  This parameter shows examples of real-world uses of the command in a variety of scenarios. 

